{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1195564-question-in-regards-to-distractions-rank-2-galliard-gift","id":1195564,"title":"Question in regards to Distractions (Rank 2 Galliard) gift.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-14T18:35:24-07:00","id":1195564,"title":"Question in regards to Distractions (Rank 2 Galliard) gift.","content":"A werewolf with the gift mentioned on the title uses it on a Mage that's been empowered by a demon (the mage is a thrall) and possesses the mental immunity aspect (the demon innate ability to be immune to all mental intrusions).<br /> <br /> The Mage also possesses a concentration merit, being able to shun out any distractions(if that even counts, just throwing it out there).<br /> <br /> Would the werewolf be able to use said gift on the Mage? or is the mage immune to it due to the demonic empowerment of mental immunity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Distractions (Level Two) \u2014 The werewolf can make distracting yips, yelps, and howls to divert the attention of his target. A coyote-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <br /> System: The player rolls Wits + Performance (difficulty equals the victim\u2019s Willpower). Each success subtracts one die from the target\u2019s dice pool for the next three turns </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T02:01:43-07:00","id":1195662,"title":"","content":"Any answers please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T02:52:34-07:00","id":1195665,"title":"","content":"I would argue, that the concentration merit would protect the mage, but the immunity to mind control wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T02:52:52-07:00","id":1195666,"title":"","content":"I see no reason for the mage not to be immune, so I would say that the mage is immune. The mage is immune to both mundane distrations and mental intrusions, and the gift is either the ability to distract a person in a mundane way or a mental intrusion, and the mage is immune to both of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13611-metalrift","name":"Metalrift","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}